  "result": "All 5 tests pass.\n\n**What I built:** `reports/render.py` with the fixed public interface. `render` looks up the format in a registry and raises `UnknownFormat` for unregistered names. `available_formats` returns the sorted registry keys. The two formats, text and markdown, are plain functions registered with a `@format_renderer` decorator, and they share small helpers for stringifying cells and joining lines. Output is newline-terminated, which is what makes the trailing blank line after the title survive the tests' `splitlines()` check when a report has no rows.\n\n**Approach:** I chose Approach B, composition with a registry. The two formats share almost no structure beyond \"stringify the cells\", so a template-method base class would have imposed hooks the renderers don't need, while a decorator-based registry keeps adding a new format to writing one function.\n\nNothing is committed. The new file is `reports/render.py`, and `tests/` is untouched.",
